## 4. Component Specifications\
\
### 4.1 SwiftUI Views Layer\
\
**Key Components:**\
- `AIAssistantOverlay.swift` - Primary chat interface overlay\
- `VoiceAssistantView.swift` - Voice interaction overlay \
- `OnboardingView.swift` - Main onboarding flow that hosts the assistant\
\
**Integration Points:**\
- Publishes current onboarding step ID to the ConversationStore\
- Displays chat messages streamed from ConversationStore\
- Reports form field changes for contextual awareness\
\
**Implementation Requirements:**\
- Display a floating "Assistant" button on all onboarding screens\
- Render chat bubbles with typing indicators for AI responses\
- Support voice input/output with appropriate animations\
- Maintain responsive design across different device sizes\
\
### 4.2 ConversationStore Layer\
\
**Key Components:**\
- `ConversationStore.swift` - Core store for chat state\
- `AIAssistantViewModel.swift` - Business logic for the assistant\
- `NetworkMonitor.swift` - Monitors connection status\
\
**Integration Points:**\
- Subscribes to SwiftUI view state changes via Combine\
- Manages conversation history with Core Data\
- Connects to Responses API via HTTPS/SSE\
\
**Implementation Requirements:**\
- Persist conversations for continuity between sessions\
- Implement retry logic for failed API requests\
- Handle offline detection and mode switching\
- Maintain message ordering and typing indicators\
\
### 4.3 Responses API\
\
**Key Components:**\
- `OpenAIService.swift` - Client-side API integration\
- Serverless functions (hosted on Supabase)\
\
**Integration Points:**\
- Makes calls to OpenAI Assistants API\
- Handles streaming responses via Server-Sent Events (SSE)\
- Processes tool calls and function invocations\
\
**Implementation Requirements:**\
- Set up OpenAI API integration with proper authentication\
- Configure streaming response handling\
- Implement function calling interface\
- Add rate limiting and error handling\
\
### 4.4 AI Model & Tools\
\
**Key Components:**\
- `ToolRegistry.swift` - Manages available tools\
- Various tool implementations (Career, Profile, etc.)\
- System prompt and function definitions\
\
**Integration Points:**\
- Connects to Supabase for data operations\
- Interfaces with SendGrid for human escalations\
- Retrieves and stores user profile data\
\
**Implementation Requirements:**\
- Implement tool classes with proper error handling\
- Define function schemas for OpenAI's function calling\
- Set up proper authentication for external services\
- Configure comprehensive system prompts\
\
### 4.5 Supabase Integration\
\
**Key Components:**\
- `SupabaseService.swift` - Client-side Supabase API wrapper\
- PostgreSQL database with pgvector extension\
- RLS (Row Level Security) policies for data protection\
\
**Integration Points:**\
- Stores and retrieves user profile information\
- Performs vector similarity search for career matching\
- Authenticates users and manages sessions\
\
**Implementation Requirements:**\
- Set up proper database schema with vector columns\
- Configure RPC functions for vector search\
- Implement Row Level Security policies\
- Set up authentication flow\
